---
title: homelab
summary: Always-on mini PC running the docker stack that replaces my SaaS dependencies.
status: active
stack: Ubuntu, Tailscale, Syncthing, Docker, chezmoi
repo: https://github.com/jplr/homelab
---

A mini PC in the office runs Jellyfin, the *arr stack, Paperless-ngx,
Syncthing, and the things that come next. Tailscale meshes it with the
laptops and phone. Chezmoi keeps every machine identical. Mullvad routes the
traffic that should be routed.

The point is not the homelab. The point is that no quarterly subscription
can take it away.
